Z||000000||JetroGT||10-10-2001||11:55 PM||||This week I've been driving around Ft.Worth and Dallas looking for a new Fiero. I found this one in Granbaury. He's asking 3300 for it. I'm only going to offer 1200. It needs motor work and the tranny is messed up. It shuts off when you put it into gear. And the kick down cable is hanging loose out of the casing. The interior looks a bit melted. Frame should be rust free. "New Mexico car"<BR>PW PL Air PT sunroof.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cropedGT1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CropedGT2.jpg"> <BR>Tommorow I'm going out to Loydes. He says he may have what I'm looking for. <BR>The search continues...<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NewSigt.jpg">  <BR>I work where all the missing paperclips go.<BR>Wanted: 86/87 Red GT, auto, pw, pl, pm, rear defrost,pt, Gray int, Spoiler. May be willing to trade the blue car.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever3000||10-11-2001||12:43 AM||||Check out my mostly-black 88GT at Southlake on Saturday.  It's not as pretty as that one, but the interior is perfect (guess I better clean it tomorrow), and runs great.  I'll be replacing the alternator soon, and I still need to find where rainwater is getting into the trunk.  67,000 miles (before Saturday anyway).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||10-11-2001||01:37 AM||||Are you selling that one? I'll be their on Sat.<BR>I must be crazy. I need another fiero like a hole in the head.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||10-11-2001||02:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Are you selling that one?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I'm <I>willing</I> to.  Need to sell <I>one</I> of them, but I've been too lazy to fill out the stuff on eBay.  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I need another fiero like a hole in the head.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>That's what a prospective buyer of my Coupe said.  He finally decided a hole in the head was not a priority right now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I can empathize with that.  Don't get too excited about my GT just yet, I'm quite fond of her and don't know if we could agree on a price (if you want it, that is).  I'll try to be realistic however.  I haven't sold a Fiero yet, I just buy em, drive em and enjoy em.  Which is why I'm going up Saturday just to hang out with other holey-heads.  It's not a case of 'I got nothing better to do', because there <B>IS</B> nothing better to do, right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> 'Cept maybe eating homemade ice cream.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||JetroGT||10-11-2001||12:45 PM||||I just talked to Loyde. He's got an 87 GT with a blown engine. He says he'll install a 3.4 and sell for around 3800. Give or take.<BR>That means I gotta work some over time. I have an extra intake and a set of valve covers. I want to do a red and black paint job on the car so I'll have to come up with that same theme for engine. Or I could just paint everything red again.||||reg||1
